<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<root BTCPP_format="4">
  <!--
    follow_person_bt.xml
    ────────────────────
    Minimal BT for person following. Recovery behaviors (Spin, Wait, BackUp)
    are intentionally removed.

    Rationale
    ─────────
    The original BT had a RecoveryNode wrapping the pipeline. When
    ComputePathToPose failed (person near a wall, brief occlusion), the
    recovery sequence fired: Spin 90° → Wait 5s → BackUp 0.3m.
    During those 5+ seconds Nav2 was locked in recovery and ignored all
    incoming NavigateToPose goals. By the time recovery finished the person
    had moved and the robot was disoriented.

    With this BT, a planning failure simply returns FAILURE on that tick.
    The BT ticks again immediately (bt_loop_duration: 10ms) with whatever
    the latest goal is — which is almost always in free space by then.

    PipelineSequence behaviour
    ──────────────────────────
    • ComputePathToPose runs at 1 Hz via RateController. It re-plans the
      global path once per second regardless of goal updates.
    • FollowPath runs every tick (10ms). It tracks the current path and
      smoothly handles the frequent goal changes at 2Hz from the follow node.
    • If either child returns FAILURE the whole sequence fails silently
      and the next tick starts fresh. No state is latched.
  -->
  <BehaviorTree ID="FollowPerson">
    <PipelineSequence>
      <RateController hz="1.0">
        <ComputePathToPose goal="{goal}" planner_id="GridBased" path="{path}"/>
      </RateController>
      <FollowPath controller_id="FollowPath" path="{path}"/>
    </PipelineSequence>
  </BehaviorTree>
</root>